# Flutter Monorepo — Cursor Rules

## Architecture

- This is a Melos monorepo. Packages live in `packages/`, apps in `apps/`.
- Apps depend on packages. Packages never depend on apps.
- Run `melos bootstrap` after any pubspec change. Never `flutter pub get` in a single package.

## Packages

- `core` — pure Dart + Flutter utilities: Result, Dio client, KeyValueStore, Environment.
- `design_system` — tokens, themes, components. No business logic.
- `logger` — pure Dart, no Flutter dependency.

## Code style

- Strict Dart: null safety, sealed classes for Result, pattern matching.
- No `print()`. Use `AppLogger`.
- Prefer `const` constructors, `final` fields, single quotes.
- Use `AppSpacing` and `AppRadius` tokens instead of magic numbers.
- Every public API has a doc comment.

## State management

- This boilerplate does not prescribe a state management framework. If one is added, document it here before writing feature code.

## Testing

- Every package has a `test/` directory mirroring `lib/`.
- Widget tests use `flutter_test`. Pure Dart tests use `package:test`.
- Run `melos run test` before opening a PR.

## Commits

- Conventional commits: `feat:`, `fix:`, `chore:`, `refactor:`, `test:`.
- Scope by package: `feat(core): add timeout retry interceptor`.
